      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Skin tone significantly affects how inflammation presents, which is a crucial point for dermatology. In darker skin tones, erythema might not appear as a bright red flush; instead, it can manifest as hyperpigmentation or dusky discoloration. Clinicians must be aware that inflammation can look different across racial groups, so relying on textbook images of white skin is often misleading. Always look for changes in texture, warmth, or palpable inflammation rather than just color.",
